---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import TalkBanner from '../components/TalkBanner.astro';
import LegalDoc from '../components/LegalDoc.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
import { withBase } from '../config/paths';

// Draft, 2026-10-27, awaiting a solicitor's review. Payment (50% deposit, 50% before launch) is
// Gurman's choice; three revision rounds, "pay once" and "pay the difference" match the pricing
// page. Keep them in step with docs/02-offer-and-pricing.md.
---

<BaseLayout page="terms">
  <SiteHeader slot="header" />

  <LegalDoc
    title="Terms and conditions"
    updated="27 October 2026"
    note="These terms are new and are awaiting review. If anything here differs from the written quote you accept, your quote applies."
  >
    <h2>1. About these terms</h2>
    <p>
      These terms apply when you hire us for a website, app, design, software or support work. Your
      written quote sets out exactly what you are getting and the price. If your quote and these
      terms disagree, your quote applies. Using the website itself is covered by our{' '}
      <a href={withBase('/user-agreement/')}>user agreement</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Quotes and prices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Before any work starts, we confirm in writing what is included and a fixed price. A quote is
        valid for 30 days.
      </li>
      <li>
        The prices on our <a href={withBase('/pricing/')}>pricing page</a> are for each tier as
        described there. Custom work and anything outside a tier is quoted separately.
      </li>
      <li>
        Websites are paid for once. There is no monthly fee unless you choose a care plan. If you
        move up a tier later, you pay only the difference between the two prices.
      </li>
      <li>
        Costs from other companies, such as your domain name, paid plugins, payment provider fees
        and AI model or API usage, are either paid by you directly or passed on at cost. We tell you
        about them before you commit.
      </li>
      <li>We are not registered for VAT, so no VAT is added to our prices.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Paying</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We ask for a 50% deposit to book your project. Work starts once it is paid.</li>
      <li>The remaining 50% is due before your site goes live or is handed over to you.</li>
      <li>
        Care plans are billed monthly in advance. What each plan includes is confirmed in writing
        when you sign up.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. What we need from you</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        The text, photos, logins and decisions the project needs, by the dates we agree at the
        start. If they arrive late, the timeline moves with them.
      </li>
      <li>
        Confirmation that you have the right to use everything you send us, such as photos, logos
        and text.
      </li>
      <li>Feedback in one place at each stage, so changes don't get lost.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Revisions and changes</h2>
    <p>
      Every tier includes three rounds of revisions. A round is one set of changes you send us
      together, which we then make. Extra rounds, or work beyond what your quote covers, are quoted
      before we do them, and we only go ahead once you agree.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Timelines</h2>
    <p>
      Timelines we give are estimates. We tell you as soon as anything changes. We are not
      responsible for delays caused by late content or feedback, or by other companies' services.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Who owns the work</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Once you have paid in full, you own your website's design and the content we create for you,
        and we hand over everything you need to run it. Until then, the work remains ours.
      </li>
      <li>
        Your domain name and accounts are set up in your name wherever possible, so they stay yours.
      </li>
      <li>
        Fonts, plugins, open-source code and other third-party tools stay under their own licences.
        We tell you about any that need a paid licence.
      </li>
      <li>
        We may show the finished work in our portfolio, unless you ask us not to. We never show
        private information or anything you ask us to keep confidential.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>8. What we don't promise</h2>
    <p>
      No one can guarantee search rankings, appearing in Google's AI Overviews or ChatGPT's answers,
      visitor numbers or sales, and we don't. We promise the work set out in your quote, done with
      reasonable care and skill, and we tell you honestly what we measure afterwards.
    </p>

    <h2>9. AI features</h2>
    <p>
      AI assistants and automations can make mistakes. Anything they say to your customers is
      approved by you before launch, they tell people they are talking to an assistant, and they
      hand over to a person when they aren't sure. If we handle your customers' personal data for
      you, for example through a booking system or an AI assistant, we agree a data processing
      agreement with you first.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Other companies' services</h2>
    <p>
      Hosting, domains, payments (such as Stripe, Square or SumUp), AI models and similar services
      are provided by other companies under their own terms. We choose them carefully, but we are
      not responsible for their outages or changes. Card details are handled by the payment provider
      and never pass through our code.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Cancelling</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        If you are buying as an individual rather than for a business, you have 14 days from
        accepting your quote to cancel without giving a reason. If you ask us to start work within
        those 14 days and then cancel, you pay for the work done up to the point you cancel.
      </li>
      <li>
        At any other time, you can stop a project by telling us in writing. You pay for the work
        done up to that point, and once it is paid for, it is yours.
      </li>
      <li>
        We may end a project if payment is more than 30 days late, or if we are asked to do
        something unlawful. We tell you in writing first.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>12. Our responsibility to you</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        If we break these terms, we are responsible for loss you suffer that was a foreseeable
        result of it.
      </li>
      <li>
        If you hire us for a business, we are not responsible for lost profits, lost sales or
        business interruption, and our total responsibility for a project is limited to the price
        you paid for it.
      </li>
      <li>
        Nothing in these terms limits responsibility for death or personal injury caused by
        negligence, for fraud, or for anything else the law doesn't allow to be limited. If you are
        a consumer, your legal rights, including those under the Consumer Rights Act 2015, are not
        affected.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>13. If something goes wrong</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a> and tell us what has
      happened. A person will reply and we will do our best to put it right.
    </p>

    <h2>14. Changes and law</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms. The version in place when you accept your quote applies to your
      project. These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales, and disputes go to the
      courts of England and Wales. If you are a consumer living in Scotland or Northern Ireland, you
      can also bring proceedings in your local courts.
    </p>
  </LegalDoc>

  <TalkBanner />

  <SiteFooter slot="footer" />
</BaseLayout>
